-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sacramento-valley.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sacramento Valley</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sacramento Valley is the northern part of California's Central Valley, drained by the Sacramento River.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sacred-cenote"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sacred-cenote.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sacred Cenote</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sacred Cenote is a large natural sinkhole at Chichen Itza in Yucatán, Mexico, linked to the city's main plaza by a raised causeway.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sacred-ensembles-of-the-hoysalas"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sacred-ensembles-of-the-hoysalas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sacred Ensembles of the Hoysalas</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sacred Ensembles of the Hoysalas is a UNESCO World Heritage Site in Karnataka, inscribed in 2023.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sacred-heart"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sacred-heart.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sacred Heart</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sacred Heart is a Roman Catholic devotion to the physical heart of Jesus as a symbol of divine love, spread widely from the seventeenth century after the visions of…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sacred-kingship"><span class="enc-name">Sacred kingship</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Sacred kingship refers to the idea that a ruler possesses divine or supernatural qualities, or acts as an intermediary between the community and the spiritual world.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sacro-catino"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sacro-catino.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sacro Catino</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sacro Catino is a green hexagonal dish kept in the treasury of San Lorenzo Cathedral in Genoa.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sacro-regio-consiglio"><span class="enc-name">Sacro Regio Consiglio</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sacro Regio Consiglio was the supreme court of the Kingdom of Naples, created by Alfonso V of Aragon after his conquest of the kingdom in 1442.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sacsayhuaman"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sacsayhuaman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sacsayhuamán</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Sacsayhuamán is an Inca complex on a hill overlooking Cusco in Peru, famous for its zigzag walls of huge, precisely fitted stone blocks.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sada-kaur"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sada-kaur.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sada Kaur</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sada Kaur was the leader of the Kanhaiya Misl, one of the Sikh confederacies, after the death of her husband Gurbakhsh Singh in 1785.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sadaham"><span class="enc-name">Sadaham</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sadaham was a young hwarang, a member of the elite youth corps of Silla, in the 6th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sadaikka-thevar"><span class="enc-name">Sadaikka Thevar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sadaikka Thevar was a Maravar chief who founded the line of the Sethupathis of Ramnad in southern Tamil Nadu.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sadaqa-ibn-mansur"><span class="enc-name">Sadaqa ibn Mansur</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sadaqa ibn Mansur was the most powerful ruler of the Mazyadid dynasty of central Iraq, an Arab Shia family.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sadashiva-raya"><span class="enc-name">Sadashiva Raya</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sadashiva Raya was emperor of Vijayanagara from 1542 to about 1570, the last ruler of the Tuluva dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sadashivrao-bhau"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sadashivrao-bhau.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sadashivrao Bhau</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sadashivrao Bhau was a Maratha general and cousin of the Peshwa Balaji Baji Rao.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Saddam Hussein</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Saddam Hussein was the Ba'athist ruler of Iraq, effective leader from the 1970s and president from 1979 to 2003.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/saddell-abbey"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/saddell-abbey.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Saddell Abbey</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Saddell Abbey is a ruined Cistercian monastery on the east coast of Kintyre in Argyll, Scotland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/en