><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Sadiya is a town in Tinsukia district in the far east of Assam, India, on the plain of the upper Brahmaputra near the border with Arunachal Pradesh.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sadocus"><span class="enc-name">Sadocus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sadocus was a son of the Odrysian king Sitalces.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sadozai"><span class="enc-name">Sadozai</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sadozai are a clan of the Popalzai branch of the Abdali or Durrani Pashtuns of Afghanistan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sadr"><span class="enc-name">Sadr</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">Sadr was a title of high office in the Safavid state of Iran.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sadras"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sadras.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sadras</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Sadras, now Sadurangapattinam, is a coastal village south of Chennai in Tamil Nadu, India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sadri-maqsudi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sadri-maqsudi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sadri Maqsudi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sadri Maqsudi was a Tatar lawyer and politician who sat in the Russian State Duma and led efforts for Muslim autonomy after the 1917 revolution.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sadriddin-ayni"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sadriddin-ayni.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sadriddin Ayni</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sadriddin Ayni (1878–1954) was a Tajik writer, poet and scholar, regarded as the founder of modern Tajik literature.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sadyattes"><span class="enc-name">Sadyattes</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sadyattes was a king of Lydia of the Mermnad dynasty, son of Ardys and father of Alyattes, who reigned in the later 7th century BCE from his capital at Sardis.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sadyr-japarov"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sadyr-japarov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sadyr Japarov</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sadyr Japarov is a Kyrgyz nationalist politician.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/saeed-bin-maktoum-al-maktoum"><span class="enc-name">Saeed bin Maktoum Al Maktoum</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Saeed bin Maktoum Al Maktoum was ruler of Dubai from 1912 to 1958.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/saeima"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/saeima.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Saeima</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Saeima is the single-chamber parliament of Latvia, made up of 100 members elected by proportional representation.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/saenz-pena-law"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/saenz-pena-law.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sáenz Peña Law</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sáenz Peña Law was the Argentine electoral law of 1912, promoted by President Roque Sáenz Peña, which established secret, universal and compulsory male suffrage for…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="